# Temporary addresses for home delivery

For depots using the [home delivery sheet](/handbook/deliveries#delivery-sheets), you can now drop a <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> at someone else's for selected deliveries, without changing the member's address.

Until now you had to overwrite the street and remember to put it back. That mixed the host into invoices and the member portal. A **temporary address** leaves the member's home address alone and only changes where the <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> is dropped.

You add it from the member page, under the contact address. One temporary address can cover several deliveries, and a member can have more than one (another host, other weeks). The name on the list stays the member's. The host appears in bold on the PDF and Excel sheets.

Members on a home-delivery depot can announce it themselves from their account, on their deliveries page, up to the same deadline as other <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> updates.

The depot's delivery-list notification email clearly flags the row with a "temporary address" and reminds to open the attachments when any drop is redirected.

More details in [the deliveries handbook](/handbook/deliveries#delivery-sheets).
